 "result": "This repo is a Flask-style framework called Tessel, with renamed APIs.\n\n**How the variables get in**\n- `src/tessel/app.py:493-501`: the Jinja environment's `globals` are set with `session=session` (plus the other proxies). Because `session` is a global, it is reachable even outside a request.\n- `src/tessel/templating.py:21` `_base_template_vars()`: this is the default context processor. It returns `{\"g\": ctx.g}` and, when `ctx.has_request`, `{\"request\": ctx.request}`, replacing the proxies with concrete objects for speed. `session` is deliberately not replaced here (`templating.py:30`).\n- `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184`: `_base_template_vars` is pre-registered as the first injector, under the `None` key (app-wide).\n- `src/tessel/app.py:588` `fill_template_scope(ctx, context)`: runs from `_render` in `templating.py:123`. It calls every injector for `None` plus the active bundles, and merges the results into the context. Values passed to `render_template` win over injector output (`app.py:607-616`).\n\n**How an app adds its own**\n- Decorator `@app.ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`). The function returns a dict and the function is appended to `template_ctx_injectors[None]`.\n- On a bundle, `@bundle.ctx_injector` applies only to that bundle's templates.\n- `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:644`) makes the variables available to every template, the same as `@app.ctx_injector`.\n- Related: `app.py:859` `shell_ctx_injector` is for the interactive shell, not templates. `sansio/app.py:825` registers template globals, which are static values and functions rather than per-render ones.",
